   "id": 399466,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which <i>two</i> public policy goals are served by granting patent rights?\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:lower-alpha\">\n<li>By protecting the property rights of inventors, the wellsprings of creation do not dry up for lack of incentive.</li>\n<li>Patent rights ensure equal treatment for all.</li>\n<li>From each according to their ability, to each according to their need.</li>\n<li>The public interest is served by disclosing the details of the invention and thereby promoting the progress of the nation.</li>\n</ol>\n",
